        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#eef4fb;font-family:system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#182d4c'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:6px solid #294b83;border-bottom:1px solid #182d4c;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>PRIMITIVE · handle</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:850 clamp(36px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.035em;text-wrap:balance;color:#182d4c'>Handle</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.4 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#46617f'>How a Port is drawn.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start;gap:32px 40px'><div style='flex:999 1 380px;min-width:0'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Meaning</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><strong>What is this thing?</strong> A Handle is how a Port is drawn. It is decoration: the Port connects, accepts and refuses exactly the same with or without it. A Port with no Handle is drawn as a plain disc with a ring and a glyph. A Handle can be set on a Port, or by the graph&#39;s root for every Port the graph exposes; the Port&#39;s own wins. A Handle is a small graph whose view holds the art (SVG, HTML or canvas), and you choose one on the Port’s card. The art is drawn whole with its centre on the border, as the plain disc is. Keep it small and quiet.</p></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #182d4c'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#182d4c'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #a6bed9'><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#46617f'>Node type</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#182d4c;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>none: a Handle is a small graph that a Port points at</dd><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#46617f'>Shown when browsing</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#182d4c;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>Yes: the art is always drawn; it takes the pointer while editing</dd><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#46617f'>Encoded as</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#182d4c;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>`handlePresentation` on a Port or node, or `defaultHandle` on the root, naming a graph whose view holds the art</dd></dl></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Invariants</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A Handle changes how a Port looks and nothing about how it behaves. Dragging, dropping and the rules for what may connect are the same with or without one.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The Port&#39;s own Handle wins over the root&#39;s default.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The root&#39;s default reaches the Ports its graph exposes and the root&#39;s own handles. It does not reach ordinary nodes inside the graph.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A Handle that cannot be reached is not an error: the Port is drawn as the plain disc.</li></ul></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Contract</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A Port or node names a Handle with <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.handlePresentation</code> (older: <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.handleRef</code>); the root names its default with <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.defaultHandle</code>, or with a <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>default-handle</code> relationship to a Portal that points at the Handle graph. The value is an address, or <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>{ sourceRef, sourceNodeId, sourcePayload }</code>, where <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>sourceNodeId</code> is the id of the root of the Handle graph.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The Handle graph&#39;s view has the payload <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>handle.web</code> and holds one of <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>svg</code>, <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>html</code> or <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>canvas</code>. It may give <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>width</code> and <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>height</code> (44 by 32 if not), a <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>hotspot</code> (the centre if not) and a <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>rotation</code>.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The art points along its own +X, and is turned so that +X faces away from the node.</li></ul></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Ports and Relationships</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A Handle is not a node in the graph that uses it, and it has no Ports of its own. The Port names it by address; nothing is drawn between them. An older <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>handle</code> relationship from a Port to a Handle was cut from the model and cannot be created.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Behavior</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>To dress a Port, press Edit on its card and choose a Handle: Plain disc, Ring or Diamond. Choosing Plain disc takes it off. To dress every Port a graph exposes, press Edit on the root and choose a default there; a Port that names its own keeps it.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A Handle that is not one of the three is left as it is. The card shows its address and does not rewrite it until you choose one.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The art is drawn whole, with its hotspot on the node&#39;s border, in the graph editor and on a workspace tile.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>While editing, every Port on every node can be dragged from, whatever it wears. While browsing, only the focused node&#39;s Ports can.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>On a workspace tile a drawn Handle stays on the border at any size, and gives way to the glyph below 6% zoom. A plain handle comes out when the tile is pointed at.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The Handle&#39;s name appears in a tooltip. A sign beside it appears only while a connection is being dragged, or on a handle that leads somewhere.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Handles on one side that would sit too close are spread along it so that their labels do not overlap.</li></ul></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Known gaps</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The type glyph is drawn over the art, which hides text in it. Art with letters in it reads badly.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The picker offers only the canon Handles. Using another still means writing its address as <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.handlePresentation</code> under Advanced, or from a Method.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Nothing checks the art&#39;s size, so a large Handle can cover its node.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A Handle graph that cannot be fetched falls back to the plain disc without saying so.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The canon smoke suite for graph-defined Handles was built before the art was drawn whole on the border, and has not been looked at since.</li></ul></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Representations</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>SVG, HTML or canvas, in the view of a small graph. The plain disc (a disc, a ring, and a glyph or a pip) is the default. Canon has two, a ring and a diamond, and a Port or a root offers them by name.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>It is not the Port. A Port is what it connects; a Handle is how it is drawn.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>It is not the node&#39;s glyph, which is the small picture standing for the whole graph.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>It is not a way to show type or direction. Colour and shape that carry meaning belong to the Port&#39;s type, not to its Handle.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>It is not a connection.</li></ul></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Examples</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The linked example is a separate graph. Inspect its relevant nodes and relationships; this specification does not embed or execute the example.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A ring and a diamond, on the borders of three cards joined by edges: one card wears a plain disc, one the ring and one the diamond. Each card connects the same way whatever it wears.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Where this lives</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Source (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/NodeGraph/graphHandlePresentation.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/NodeGraph/GraphHandleVisual.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/NodeGraph/HandleLayer.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/NodeGraph/handleSpread.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/NodeGraph/handleVisibility.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/workspaceCapabilities.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/components/WorkspaceLayer.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Focused tests (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/graphHandlePresentation.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/handleDrag.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/handleSpread.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/handleVisibility.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/workspaceCapabilities.test.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>These pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='primary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:12px;border-top:3px solid #294b83'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:750 26px/1.1 system-ui;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#182d4c'>Handle example</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#46617f'>A worked example: primitives/handle/example.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/primitives/handle/example/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#294b83'>Open the example →</a></section></div></div></div></div></div>"
        },
